IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cbr-nouns`
IMPORT `cbr-reg3`

-- TESTS OF REGULATION 3 (src:52-58). Expected values are written from the text: "if the
-- amount of child benefit which would have been payable under those Regulations
-- would, by virtue of the relevant transitional provisions and savings (had they
-- remained in force), be greater than the amount prescribed by these Regulations,
-- the greater amount shall be payable."
--
-- The amount under the 1976 Regulations is out of text, so each case supplies it.
-- Amounts are pounds a week.

§ `Tests of regulation 3`

§§ `Regulation 3(1) (src:52-55): the greater amount`

-- The earlier amount is greater than the amount these Regulations prescribe: it is payable.
#ASSERT `the greater amount payable under regulation 3(1)` 17.90 (JUST 20.00) EQUALS 20.00
#ASSERT `the greater amount payable under regulation 3(1)` 27.05 (JUST 30.00) EQUALS 30.00
-- One penny greater: still the greater amount.
#ASSERT `the greater amount payable under regulation 3(1)` 27.05 (JUST 27.06) EQUALS 27.06
-- Equal: not greater, and the amount is the same either way.
#ASSERT `the greater amount payable under regulation 3(1)` 27.05 (JUST 27.05) EQUALS 27.05
-- One penny less: the amount these Regulations prescribe.
#ASSERT `the greater amount payable under regulation 3(1)` 27.05 (JUST 27.04) EQUALS 27.05
#ASSERT `the greater amount payable under regulation 3(1)` 17.90 (JUST 11.70) EQUALS 17.90
-- No transitional provision or saving would have applied: the amount these Regulations prescribe stands.
#ASSERT `the greater amount payable under regulation 3(1)` 17.90 NOTHING EQUALS 17.90
#ASSERT `the greater amount payable under regulation 3(1)` 27.05 NOTHING EQUALS 27.05

§§ `Regulation 3(1) applied to a weekly rate that may itself be not covered`

#ASSERT `the weekly amount payable after the saving in regulation 3` (JUST 17.90) (JUST 20.00) EQUALS JUST 20.00
#ASSERT `the weekly amount payable after the saving in regulation 3` (JUST 27.05) (JUST 20.00) EQUALS JUST 27.05
#ASSERT `the weekly amount payable after the saving in regulation 3` (JUST 27.05) NOTHING EQUALS JUST 27.05
-- Where the amount these Regulations prescribe is not covered, the greater amount is not known either: NOTHING stays NOTHING.
#ASSERT `the weekly amount payable after the saving in regulation 3` NOTHING (JUST 50.00) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the weekly amount payable after the saving in regulation 3` NOTHING NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Regulation 3(2) (src:56-58): the relevant transitional provisions and savings`

#ASSERT `the relevant transitional provisions and savings for` `child benefit payable under SSCBA` EQUALS `regulations 3 and 4 of the Child Benefit and Social Security (Fixing and Adjustment of Rates) (Amendment) Regulations 1998`
#ASSERT `the relevant transitional provisions and savings for` `child benefit payable under SSCB(NI)A` EQUALS `regulations 3 and 4 of the Child Benefit and Social Security (Fixing and Adjustment of Rates) (Amendment) Regulations (Northern Ireland) 1998`

§§ `The two instruments regulation 3(1) names (src:52-54)`

#ASSERT count `the earlier Regulations named in regulation 3(1)` EQUALS 2
